release fist a technique that bang  sealed off long ago for people who read  the webcomic and think that they don't  need to read the manga this is another  prime example of how the two can be very  different not only are the illustrations  next level but new stuff is added or  changed all the time like this very  intriguing backstory of bang and the  explosion fist which by the way matches  his name bang beautifully we're told  that when garl was fleeing he broke into  the dojo and looked at the scrolls bang  ensured he couldn't escape with them but  garo being the genius he is got a grasp  of it with just one read furthermore  bang calls it a wicked technique which  adds the curiosity even more so this is  perfect characterization time for bang  here as he says to think i'd have to  settle things with garo as well as with  my past self at the same time he's even  more certain that he must not lose now  we then get the much needed and  appreciated backstory that will probably  shock a lot of us that bang used to be  an out of control ruffian in his youth  in fact he's almost a spitting image of  garo in the flashback in looks and  behavior he challenged anyone who looked  strong and sent them to the hospital he  also had such a smug smirk on his face  the perfect cocky douchebag expression i  must say he was drowning in martial arts  talent we're told which is a fantastic  way of putting it and he clearly had  girls and money to go with it he was the  picture of carnal desires rather than  discipline he enjoyed martial arts by  doing what he felt like and when his  brother tried to talk some sense into  him bang said his big bro was getting  bald because he was so rock headed we're  reintroduced to young bang as explosion  released fist wind of blood bang which  by the way how awesome is that name this  is making me love bang all the more  knowing he had this interesting  backstory his big bro let him know that  he was losing hair because of stress and  said he's here to cut the stress off at  the source which is obviously his out of  control little brother by the way bomb's  full title was whirlwind iron cutting  fist wind of death bomb another cool  name definitely a very cool family  overall bomb challenges bang telling him  his rampage will end here and as bang  shoots away the girls he prepares to  fight bang tells his brother that his  die hard training day in and day out is  absurd believing that he is unbeatable  because he's a guy with good taste  having fun not sure if i ever heard that  reason for being unbeatable but  interesting nonetheless it's a clear  conflict between discipline committing  to a process whether you like it or not  and bang's fun approach which includes  using power to just enjoy oneself that  way even though he's doing constant  martial arts by beating people up he has  zero stress according to him his form of  martial arts is pretty much losing  himself in fighting people again  emphasizing his lack of discipline bomb  even says bang thinks he gains so much  power but he hasn't even overcome  himself and then he says he'll teach him  a lesson about that and lo and behold  discipline in mastering one's desires  wins out bomb badly defeats bang and i  guess it's not a surprise since clearly  balding is a sign of strength in one  punch man just look at saitama bang  understood that while his fist was  filled with killing intent his brother  had none and yet bang still lost that's  how outmatched he was and how inferior  his so-called training was to bombs he  could sense that he lost because he was  too close-minded in his ways and needed  to be more broad-minded he sealed off  the explosion release fist and trained  many years now like bomb not against  opponents per se but with himself and  thus was born the ultimate defense of  art the water stream rock smashing fist  like his brother he opened the dojo and  his brother was glad to see it i love  the brother dynamic here by the way it's  absolutely awesome and bomb lets us know  that bang became a hero despite having  no interest in it sort of telling bomb  that he's reformed himself he's no  longer a dude who just does what he  feels like when bomb heard about bang  trying to confront a former student he  felt like bang was trying to do exactly  what bomb did for him trying to reform  his student rather than just destroy him  and i think this makes so much more  sense now now that we got this backstory  it really helped flesh out bang's  motivation otherwise it would have been  hard to believe he'd be so willing to go  easy on garo in the past and give him  chance after chance if he wasn't in the  exact same situation before and had  someone to help reform him he's more  certain that he can reform garo because  he was garo in the past or at least very  similar to him bomb wanted to help  worried that bang's resolve might be  misplaced bang insisted that this was  between master and student and so bam  made up the excuse that garo may go  after his dojo to join his brother as  his elder brother bomb followed what he  felt was his duty and i gotta say i have  a newfound appreciation for his  character too after all of this new  information very good chapter in that  sense in the present bomb sees that bang  is being overwhelmed but he also sees  that garo's technique is incomplete he  thinks that bang's only chance is the  explosion release fist but bang doesn't  use it when he gets the opening he is  officially a man of principles now not  willing to win if it means winning the  wrong way and embracing the past he's  renounced and bomb smiles seeing how far  bang has come and that he is in fact  fully reformed in a far cry from the man  he used to be i did wonder why explosion  fist would work against garo potentially  if it didn't even work against bomb in  the past but perhaps bomb's technique  was more complete and he didn't allow  any openings for it to be used as garo  does bang gets smashed to the ground and  he's clearly very beat up and sweaty but  he doesn't give up and even says looks  like i'm getting through watch carefully  big bro end quote it's a  goosebump-inducing moment but also kind  of funny because you're thinking how  does he know it's getting through to  garo when gar was beating him up  mercilessly but you know that bang knows  what he's talking about when it comes to  martial arts and fighting bomb says yeah  he's watching and he sees a twisted punk  that has improved splendidly obviously  referring to bang and that fact alone  gives them both hope that garo might not  be too far gone either bang continues  fighting and i love the fact that he's  communicating through his fists he says  anyone of garo's level of talent should  be able to hear the voice of his fists  and understand him the love for martial  arts in general is really coming through  in this chapter bang acknowledges his  faults he failed as a master and let the  hero world distract him away from the  relationship with his students and so  garo went down the wrong path then his  students left the dojo and garo caused  trouble for so many heroes bang blames  himself for all of it and that's why  this battle is so significant to him  he's trying to right all of garo's  wrongs and his own and then he drops the  bang show he says after this incident  he'll retire from being a hero so we  have the end of s-class hero rank 3 bang  insane and even if he does stop being a  hero i really hope he'll stay in the  story love this character so much bang's  plan is to go back to him and garo being  master and disciple and this time he  won't let stuff like being a hero come  in the way it really does seem like he's  getting through togaro in a sense as  garo's shell literally starts cracking  we then again see genos getting wrecked  by black asses and tatsumaki too  tatsumaki seems totally powerless to do  anything at this point not even move  genos for his part only manages to get  rid of three black s's while there's  almost 4.5 billion left and i assume  that's not counting the much stronger  golden s either that absorbed a bunch of  them the situation is hopeless as far as  genos can tell he shows that he's grown  as a character too though despite not  being able to overpower the black s's  and says before he would have  self-destructed despite the heroes  around but now he uses the strength he  has left to cover and protect tatsumaki  he feels like he's not becoming stronger  because he's getting wrecked by his  enemies but still respect for his  selfless actions and for protecting  others like a true hero up to what as  far as he's concerned could be his very  last moment then as it looks like the  black s's are about to finish them off  suddenly some light appears in the  distance and surprises the black s's  which in my view must be saitama blast  and flashy flash coming to the rescue it  would definitely be perfect timing for  that but let me know if you think it  might be something else anyways wow  great chapter but the next one should be  even more hype with saitama showing up  and perhaps even blasts stopping by as  he drops them off it's definitely about  time for them to show up but they've  definitely done a good job of keeping it  interesting before they got here as well  but anyways let me know what you thought  of this chapter and what you are most  looking forward to seeing happening next  who was your mvp this time around  obviously if anyone says genos i get it  he deserved it too but i gotta give it  to bang his effort and character arc  it's been amazing learning more about  him this chapter if you did enjoy this  video and want to keep them coming you  know what to do channel the saitama  within and one punch that like button  remember smashing that like button is  s-class energy and passing is pure ugly  energy so choose wisely don't be if  you're ugly if you haven't make this the  video you subscribe and this is crucial  hi